  "name": null,
  "problem": "A smartphone app monitors the number of new subscribers, $S(t)$, in thousands, each day since its launch. The following table shows the rate at which new subscriptions are arriving.\n\n| **$t\\,\\text{(days)}$** | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${S}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{(thousands/day)}$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $2$ | $5.5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nAt the time $t=6,$ the app had $4$ thousand subscribers. Use the tangent line approximation of $S$ at time $t=6$ to approximate the number of subscriptions at $t=7.$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
